Simpler: store the body as `[]func(*forth) error`, where a number becomes `func(f *forth) error { f.push(n); return nil }`.

Definition parsing:
- Expect `:` then name then tokens until `;`.
- If name parses as a number → error "cannot redefine a number".
- If `;` is not found → error.

Word lookup: user-defined words take priority (overriding built-ins): check the user words map first, then built-ins.

Case-insensitive: lowercase all word names.

Division: integer division, error on divide by zero.

Stack errors: "empty stack" / "only one value on the stack".

